---
import PageLayout from '../../layouts/PageLayout.astro';

/**
 * One page, and the page is the diagram.
 *
 * Everything the argument needs is labelled inside the SVG, so there is no
 * prose beneath it and nothing to click open. Two variants, wide and narrow,
 * swapped by media query, and every label change has to land in both.
 * `diagramAlt` is the only text equivalent, so it has to stay in step too.
 *
 * No JavaScript. Longer treatments get their own pages later, and the material
 * for them already sits in `philosophyNodes[].sections` in the data file.
 */

const diagramAlt =
  'One system in four layers. At the top, the north star: No Human Left Behind, technology, ethics, and humanity evolving together. An arrow labelled The Lift rises toward it, AI-assisted work that elevates everyone. Below that, the frameworks: a closed loop of four delivery stages. Requirements carries Shift Left, requirements, standards, and the test plan, up front. Build carries Encoding Intent, judgment goes in first and the model builds from it. Testing and audit carries The Four Lenses, does the tool serve the people it touches. Retro carries Capturing What Worked, encode what worked and what failed before it fades. A dashed prevention return runs from retro back to requirements, so every failure becomes a rule, a test, or a doc. The whole loop rests on Documentation as a System, the constant underneath every stage, which every stage reads from and writes back to. Inside it runs a one-way chain: teams write it and own the structure that fits how they work, which produces the gold source, the docs humans read, versioned, reviewed, and treated as code. From that gold source, and only in that direction, skills are derived and never duplicated, one gold copy for two audiences in that order, sized for an agent to load, regenerated when the source changes and never hand-edited. At the bottom, the infrastructure that keeps it true: human-in-the-loop keeps humans in the decision, das performs the derivation, and cpm keeps the standards in sync.';
---

<PageLayout
  title="Philosophy"
  description="A north star, a delivery loop, and the documentation system underneath it. One gold copy that people write and people read, with the agent view derived from it."
>
  <article class="phil" data-philosophy>
